                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "50df3c5d-5068-41d2-bf55-b24e7f8ecd03",
                        "source_entry_id": "e3871bbb-a5cd-3f4c-b89d-661a5440c9a3",
                        "source_sense_id": "d118a9e5-3fae-3c55-af63-4c3be296fc30",
                        "source_sense_description": "Musik: die Töne einer Melodienfolge sollen ineinander übergehen",
                        "target_lang_word": "legato",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "legato",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8be5f30d-87a2-35cd-ae6d-89b84b8c2382",
                                        "entry_id": "7ad6b85f-0868-3308-ac2b-e54a5c2b66db",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Smoothly, in a connected manner."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b4cdc9fb-4bb4-4a8c-8e10-6e7cfe8716a3",
                                                "sense_id": "8be5f30d-87a2-35cd-ae6d-89b84b8c2382",
                                                "text": "Play this passage legato, not portato."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "legato",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7e2d06bb-46c2-3eec-a910-3ba1dd0c09bc",
                                        "entry_id": "99b58ebf-1799-30e8-bebc-816347ba319a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A style of performance characterized by smoothly connected notes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7a61b87b-ac20-4e4d-96fe-956c835c6f43",
                                                "sense_id": "7e2d06bb-46c2-3eec-a910-3ba1dd0c09bc",
                                                "text": "It is the coördination of the finger and hand as examplified in the proportionate speed of shifting according to the speed of the musical passage, which makes for evenness, continuity, smoothness, and ultimately, a fine legato."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b4c00856-671a-43e6-9a6a-4e84fd5dfadb",
                                                "sense_id": "7e2d06bb-46c2-3eec-a910-3ba1dd0c09bc",
                                                "text": "At the end of the prelude of Caprice V, there is a chromatic ascending and descending scale of forty-eight notes to be played in one bow in legato."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a11b3b33-cf44-44e4-9e9b-a86f6e2223b4",
                                                "sense_id": "7e2d06bb-46c2-3eec-a910-3ba1dd0c09bc",
                                                "text": "Clementi, in his \"Introduction to the art of playing the piano-forte\" (1801) still had to advise pianists that : \"the best general rule is to keep the keys of the instrument suppressed during the whole length of the note\" (p.8) and \"whenver the composer leaves the legato or staccato to the taste of the performer, the best rule is to use the legato in most cases and to reserve the staccato in order to give particular passages more spirit and to enhance the higher beauties of the legato.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b3c5c07b-c736-3d82-ab93-e49985d8b638",
                                        "entry_id": "99b58ebf-1799-30e8-bebc-816347ba319a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A passage that is played legato."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "01ce3442-c206-4b39-8ab2-1a76e26ef4d0",
                                                "sense_id": "b3c5c07b-c736-3d82-ab93-e49985d8b638",
                                                "text": "It schools the mind to watch for the legato all the time, as its absence at the organ is mor prominent than at the piano; but beyond this point it renders little assitance to the pianist."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "904e4c64-b8b7-4d6f-a2ce-1fa84a8b5662",
                                                "sense_id": "b3c5c07b-c736-3d82-ab93-e49985d8b638",
                                                "text": "A good pianist, however, will make his audience believe that he is as capable of performing a legato as is a singer or violinist."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8533e519-5009-4bd2-8e99-2af19b2f4790",
                                                "sense_id": "b3c5c07b-c736-3d82-ab93-e49985d8b638",
                                                "text": "Legatos are indicated in both notations by a bow between respective notes."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "60d3bce1-0a02-40af-94c7-b0bd7e5b7e44",
                        "source_entry_id": "e3871bbb-a5cd-3f4c-b89d-661a5440c9a3",
                        "source_sense_id": "d118a9e5-3fae-3c55-af63-4c3be296fc30",
                        "source_sense_description": "Musik: die Töne einer Melodienfolge sollen ineinander übergehen",
                        "target_lang_word": "legato",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "legato",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9e2dbf29-fd96-3c7a-9313-145d01aceb04",
                                        "entry_id": "ca533021-7408-3a0c-a84e-5e50afb89faf",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Mis en tête d’un passage, indique qu’il faut en lier les notes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0a272348-737f-4f0f-9020-9507ff87eeb9",
                                                "sense_id": "9e2dbf29-fd96-3c7a-9313-145d01aceb04",
                                                "text": "Le legato, ou liaison d’expression, indique que les notes doivent être liées : ce qui signifie qu’elles doivent couler les unes après les autres de façon continue, sans interruption du son."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b3b43d8d-06d4-4ed4-b984-8076d831849e",
                                                "sense_id": "9e2dbf29-fd96-3c7a-9313-145d01aceb04",
                                                "text": "À part cela, les phrasés sont lissés en de gros legatos (action conjuguée de Mozart et du chef), certains airs changent de titulaire (par ex. « Rejoice » par le ténor) et, surtout, l’impact choral est minoré par l’utilisation d’un schéma faisant d’abord intervenir le quatuor de solistes puis la masse chorale."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "12948a47-7ebe-4192-8a18-a76542e64226",
                                                "sense_id": "9e2dbf29-fd96-3c7a-9313-145d01aceb04",
                                                "text": "La pianiste joue avec les autres, dialoguant avec le pupitre d’altos, réagissant aux appels de cors, avant de déployer tout à coup l’orbe d’un legato tombé du ciel."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
